    },
    {
     "cue": "extra memory",
     "line": 6,
     "inside": true,
     "text": "O(n) extra memory",
     "tone": "warn"
    }
   ],
   "say": "Here is the code. Sort the left half, sort the right half, then merge. The merge walks both halves with i and j, always taking the smaller front into a temp vector. Notice the less-or-equal: when two values tie, the left one wins. That makes merge sort stable, so equal items keep their order. The price is O of n extra memory."
